Junjo is a monorepo with per-package licensing. The license for each package
is the LICENSE file in that package's directory, which is authoritative.

Summary (see each package's LICENSE for the actual terms):

  packages/sdk         MIT                  (client SDK)
  packages/react       MIT                  (React hooks)
  packages/shared      MIT                  (shared types)
  packages/sdk-roblox  MIT                  (Roblox Luau client)
  packages/server      Elastic License 2.0  (the Junjo server)
  apps/dashboard       All rights reserved  (the cloud admin dashboard)
  apps/docs            MIT                  (documentation site)

In plain terms: the client libraries are MIT and safe to use in any game,
commercial or not. The server is source-available under ELv2 - you can read
it, run it, and self-host it for your own games, but you may not offer it to
third parties as a hosted or managed service. The hosted dashboard is
proprietary.

